asis for the GA release.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix — this epic\n    delivers that requirement in full.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The supported configuration matrix's final content depends on the limits\n  and configurations validated by the parallel stability and hardening work;\n  finalize the matrix after those validations complete (an acceptance-criterion\n  gate, not a start-order dependency).\n- SLO targets and the backport policy require support/product sign-off — a\n  human process gate that may add elapsed time beyond the engineering work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40678,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b86bd42afe1f5c82","agent_id":"a010aafae814811f7","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"846097e3-36dd-4879-b068-bc117ccf022a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:15:11.836Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
