h is covered\n  by a passing test.\n- Fail-mode behavior of the integration (guardrails service unavailable or\n  degraded) is tested and documented, including the recovery path.\n- Integration documentation suitable for GA distributions is published\n  (enablement, supported configurations, failure behavior).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions — this epic\n  delivers that requirement in full.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This epic's work spans two components: the TrustyAI service side (owned by\n  the TrustyAI team) and the Llama Stack distribution wiring; the single\n  most-relevant component is TrustyAI, and cross-team coordination with the\n  Llama Stack distribution work is required.\n- The integration must build against the stability-guaranteed API surface, so\n  this work serializes after the API stability work; starting earlier would\n  validate against a surface that may still change.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41980,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b86bd42afe1f5c82","agent_id":"a010aafae814811f7","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"33f78939-632b-4e48-ad1c-30743fdf7415","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:15:20.741Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
