{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b49f7f2f7b108ebb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's defining unknown: no systematic GA-readiness\n30\tassessment of Llama Stack has been done, and TP-era feedback is scattered\n31\tacross support tickets. The epic produces the definitive GA-readiness\n32\tassessment — a gap inventory across the four categories named by the strategy\n33\t(API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) — comparing\n34\tcurrent Tech Preview quality against the GA bar. Its output is the definitive\n35\tGA scope that the stability and hardening implementation work is sized and\n36\tshaped against.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Aggregate and systematically review TP feedback from support tickets, mapped\n41\t  to gap items in the assessment.\n42\t- Assess current API stability against GA requirements (surface inventory,\n43\t  versioning state, breaking-change exposure).\n44\t- Assess upgrade paths from recent TP releases (what breaks, what is untested).\n45\t- Assess scale limits (documented vs. actual, untested ranges).\n46\t- Assess error handling quality against GA expectations.\n47\t- For each gap: severity, proposed remediation, and size estimate.\n48\t- Produce the definitive GA scope document, ratified by product and support\n49\t  stakeholders as the commitment baseline for graduation.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A written GA-readiness assessment exists covering all four gap categories\n54\t  (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), each with\n55\t  current state, GA bar, and identified gaps.\n56\t- Every identified gap item is enumerated with a severity, a proposed\n57\t  remediation, and a size estimate.\n58\t- TP feedback from support tickets has been systematically reviewed and each\n59\t  relevant item is traceable to a gap entry in the assessment (or explicitly\n60\t  dispositioned as out of scope).\n61\t- The assessment is published and accepted by the strategy owner as the\n62\t  definitive GA scope for graduation.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current\n67\t  TP quality and GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope — this epic is the\n68\t  assessment itself.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97bdaeacf2e590b1","agent_id":"a3bcbd58764a7d2ae","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"b4e929f5-c8c9-444f-b6db-2259a8ab009d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:17:34.279Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b49f7f2f7b108ebb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
