{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3059d2d564e9638","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Close inventoried GA gaps in Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: add_remediation\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the assessment finds the gap set smaller than estimated, descope\n15\t    remediation items accordingly; if larger, absorb additional items here or split\n16\t    by sub-system, re-baselining the GA scope with stakeholders.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: -1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Close inventoried GA gaps in Llama Stack\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic closes the quality gaps that the GA-readiness assessment inventories\n39\tbetween current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar — the remediation work\n40\tthat TP status currently excuses. Its contents are defined by the assessment's\n41\tfindings (expected to concentrate in error handling, scale limits, and\n42\tstability hardening), which is why it cannot be sized or started before the\n43\tassessment lands.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Remediate every gap item the GA-readiness assessment marks as blocking GA,\n48\t  following each item's proposed remediation.\n49\t- Error-handling gaps: bring error behavior in the identified surfaces up to\n50\t  the GA bar defined by the assessment.\n51\t- Scale-limit gaps: close identified scale deficiencies and validate the\n52\t  documented scale limits.\n53\t- Stability hardening items surfaced by the assessment beyond the named API\n54\t  stability deliverables.\n55\t- Each remediation carries a test demonstrating the gap is closed against the\n56\t  assessment's pass criteria.\n57\t- Re-run the failing items from the assessment's gap inventory to record\n58\t  closure.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Every gap item the GA-readiness assessment marks as GA-blocking is\n63\t  remediated, and each remediation passes the assessment's own pass criterion\n64\t  for that item.\n65\t- Error-handling and scale-limit gaps identified by the assessment are closed\n66\t  and verified by the tests attached to their remediations.\n67\t- The updated gap inventory records every item as closed (or explicitly\n68\t  re-scoped with stakeholder sign-off recorded in the assessment document).\n69\t- The existing build pipeline for the Llama Stack midstream repository remains\n70\t  green for all changes introduced by this epic.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: GA-readiness assessment producing the definitive GA scope —\n75\t  this epic delivers the gap-closure half of that requirement (the assessment\n76\t  identifies the scope; this epic closes it to the GA bar).\n77\t\n78\t## Risks / Notes\n79\t\n80\t- Sizing is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; if the\n81\t  assessment finds the gap set larger than estimated, the additional\n82\t  remediation items are absorbed here or split out by sub-system at that\n83\t  point.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97bdaeacf2e590b1","agent_id":"a3bcbd58764a7d2ae","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"8f99f0a1-ea76-474b-a685-b57d9e1e582c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:17:35.051Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3059d2d564e9638","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"sub