{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b634a929de2fc03b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n3\ttitle: API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the assessment finds the API stability surface in worse shape\n15\t    than estimated, extend the hardening scope of the versioned surface and upgrade-path\n16\t    tests accordingly; the named HLR-2 deliverables (versioned APIs, deprecation policy,\n17\t    tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases) are committed regardless and\n18\t    do not shrink.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic puts a stability guarantee on Llama Stack's published API surface so\n41\tenterprise customers can build production GenAI applications against it: the\n42\tAPI surface is versioned, a deprecation policy is published and applied, and a\n43\ttested upgrade path from the last two TP releases is delivered. This is the\n44\tcore GA commitment named by HLR-2.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Version the published API surface (the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n49\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD surface) per the platform's versioning approach.\n50\t- Author and publish a deprecation policy for the API surface, consistent with\n51\t  the GA stability guarantee.\n52\t- Apply the deprecation policy: any API slated for removal or change is marked\n53\t  and communicated per the policy rather than silently broken.\n54\t- Build and test the upgrade path from the last two TP releases, including a\n55\t  documented upgrade procedure.\n56\t- Adjust scope to any API-stability or upgrade-path findings from the\n57\t  GA-readiness assessment (the assessment's findings on these categories\n58\t  define the full extent of hardening this surface needs).\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- The published API surface is versioned and the versioning is documented.\n63\t- A deprecation policy is published, and every deprecated or changed API on\n64\t  the surface is marked and communicated per that policy.\n65\t- The upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases is exercised by an\n66\t  automated test and passes, with a documented upgrade procedure.\n67\t- A published API stability guarantee statement covers the versioned surface.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n72\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n73\t  two TP releases — this epic delivers that requirement in full.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- The published REST API surface originates upstream; aligning versioning and\n78\t  deprecation semantics may require coordination with the upstream project,\n79\t  which could extend the timeline.\n80\t- Per the strategy's open question, the size of the stability work is an\n81\t  estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is gated on that\n82\t  assessment and its scope may be rewritten by its findings.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97bdaeacf2e590b1","agent_id":"a3bcbd58764a7d2ae","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"115462eb-3ed4-4830-9ce8-ad09b9bfa671",