of the support posture from the accountable\n51\t  support and product stakeholders.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- SLO targets for the GA component are documented and reviewed by the\n56\t  accountable support stakeholders.\n57\t- The backport policy is documented and reviewed by the accountable support\n58\t  stakeholders.\n59\t- The supported configuration matrix is documented, and every entry in it\n60\t  corresponds to a configuration validated by the GA stability, upgrade-path,\n61\t  or hardening work (no unvalidated claims).\n62\t- The support posture documentation is accepted as the production support\n63\t  basis for the GA release.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n68\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix — this epic\n69\t    delivers that requirement in full.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- The supported configuration matrix's final content depends on the limits\n74\t  and configurations validated by the parallel stability and hardening work;\n75\t  finalize the matrix after those validations complete (an acceptance-criterion\n76\t  gate, not a start-order dependency).\n77\t- SLO targets and the backport policy require support/product sign-off — a\n78\t  human process gate that may add elapsed time beyond the engineering work.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97bdaeacf2e590b1","agent_id":"a3bcbd58764a7d2ae","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"fe1d6572-abb5-405d-afcb-8f016c935776","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:17:36.736Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afd14d6c155c6a6b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
