h-ups\n49\t  only, no new content.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- On an entitled cluster, Llama Stack management is available in the Dashboard\n54\t  with no opt-in configuration change required.\n55\t- On a cluster without the relevant entitlement, Llama Stack management is not\n56\t  enabled.\n57\t- The default can be reverted or overridden through configuration, and that\n58\t  override path is tested.\n59\t- The existing Dashboard test suite passes, with tests updated to cover the\n60\t  new default behavior.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- **HLR-5 (P1)**: The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n65\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate) — this epic delivers that requirement\n66\t  in full.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97bdaeacf2e590b1","agent_id":"a3bcbd58764a7d2ae","session_id":"39957edc-33e6-45f5-8209-165342cd81d6","uuid":"2fb9eeea-1bf2-4513-ada7-c483786fbd72","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:17:37.809Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ac510a815721102","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
