me (a standalone fail-mode Investigation would fail the Rule 4 test).\n70\tNo missing data/artifact dependencies were found in epic content beyond those\n71\thandled as AC gates above.\n72\t\n73\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n74\t\n75\tEach epic carries a single canonical component and team, all matching the\n76\tarchitecture-context owning teams (Llama Stack/RHOAI GenAI, TrustyAI/TrustyAI,\n77\tDashboard/RHOAI Dashboard — verified against `.context`). E005's span across\n78\tthe TrustyAI service side and Llama Stack distribution wiring is one logical\n79\tchange (promoting one integration to supported status), with the\n80\tsingle-most-relevant component choice documented in Health Warnings and the\n81\tepic's Risks/Notes. E002's unknown sizing is handled per the one-logical-change\n82\tshape: estimate, rationale, and a concrete conditional re-split trigger\n83\t(\"absorbed here or split out by sub-system\") are all present across\n84\t`gate_failure_impact`, Risks/Notes, and Health Warnings — watch item only.\n85\tNo scope duplication: the E002/E003 boundary is explicitly drawn (E002 takes\n86\thardening \"beyond the named API stability deliverables\"), and the E005/E007\n87\tdocumentation overlap is the standard component-technical-docs → GA-docs-uplift\n88\trelationship (E007 depends on E005 and is reviewed against implemented\n89\tbehavior — not an independent rebuild of the same surface). No work-product\n90\ttype mixing: E004 is uniformly support-posture work; E005's integration\n91\tdocumentation is intrinsic to HLR-4's \"supported, documented integration\"\n92\trequirement; E006's caption/label touch-ups are correctly folded in as\n93\tincidental documentation per Rule 2's exception.\n94\t\n95\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n96\t\n97\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (the definitive GA scope) changes\n98\twhat E002 contains (`add_remediation`) and rewrites E003's scope (`rewrite`) —\n99\tthe Rule 3 decision test is met. Both gated epics have `gated_by` set, point\n100\tat an epic in their direct `dependencies` list, and carry `gate_failure_impact`\n101\twith both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated. No other epic lists an\n102\tInvestigation in `dependencies`, so no missing `gated_by` exists. All six\n103\tImplementation epics produce concrete artifacts (assessment-driven remediations,\n104\tversioned APIs and policies, support-posture documents, validated integration,\n105\ta default flip with tested override, published GA documentation). Signal field\n106\ttypes match epic types (E001 carries `investigation_signals`; all others carry\n107\t`ai_signals`).\n108\t\n109\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n110\t\n111\tAll seven ai-signals files exist, and every frontmatter signal value matches\n112\tits rationale-table value (verified signal-by-signal for all 7 epics). Signal\n113\tvalues are consistent with the strategy content: E002/E003 `open_questions: -1`\n114\tmatching their assessment gates; E004 `existing_foundation: 0` for greenfield\n115\tsupport-posture artifacts and `human_process_gates: -1` matching the sign-off\n116\trequirement; E006's favorable profile matching a precisely-specified default\n117\tflip. The `architecture_claims: +1` calibration was checked against `.context`:\n118\tllama-stack.md confirms Tech Preview maturity, the LlamaStackDistribution CRD,\n119\tand the OpenAI-compatible REST surface; trustyai.md confirms the guardrails\n120\tcapability and Dashboard-consumed metrics API; dashboard.md confirms the\n121\tOdhDashboardConfig feature-flag mechanism — every cited rationale is accurate.\n122\t\n123\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n124\t\n125\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from its HLR. Rule-mandated ACs are\n126\tpresent: E006 (a default/replacement change) has the tested\n127\trollback/override AC (Rule 23); E007 has the technically-reviewed-against-\n128\timplementation AC with recorded sign-off (Rule 24); E002 carries a\n129\tbuild-pipeline-green AC